    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterMaintenance" xml:space="preserve">Maintenance</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterMigration" xml:space="preserve">Migration</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterSetupIntro" xml:space="preserve">Point ImageRotater at what it needs from elsewhere. Each item unlocks a feature; the plugin works without any of them, it just does less.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterSteamGridDB" xml:space="preserve">SteamGridDB</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterSteamGridDBHelp" xml:space="preserve">Curated game artwork. Get a free key from steamgriddb.com under Preferences → API and paste it here. Without it, the search dialog still has Steam and web image search.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterApiKey" xml:space="preserve">API key</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterApiKeyStorage" xml:space="preserve">Stored in Playnite's settings file as plain text. The key only grants read access to public artwork and can be regenerated on SteamGridDB at any time.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterFfmpeg" xml:space="preserve">ffmpeg</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterFfmpegHelp" xml:space="preserve">Converts animated GIFs to MP4 - markedly smaller, and played by hardware rather than decoded frame by frame on the UI thread. Not bundled: ffmpeg is GPL-licensed and this plugin is MIT, so shipping the binary would change the licence of the whole project.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterYtDlp" xml:space="preserve">yt-dlp</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterYtDlpHelp" xml:space="preserve">Imports video from YouTube and similar sites as animated backgrounds and covers. Needs ffmpeg as well, which converts the download into the MP4 the plugin plays, and deno below to read YouTube at all. Also not bundled, for the same reason.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterDeno" xml:space="preserve">deno</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterDenoHelp" xml:space="preserve">yt-dlp's JavaScript runtime. YouTube hides its streams behind challenges that have to be solved by running JavaScript, and yt-dlp hands that to deno. Without it a YouTube search returns nothing, with no error to say why. Get it from deno.com, or put deno.exe next to yt-dlp.exe and both are found together.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterToolPathHint" xml:space="preserve">Leave a path blank and the plugin looks on your PATH. Set one explicitly if you keep the tool somewhere else.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterBrowse" xml:space="preserve">Browse…</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterGeneralIntro" xml:space="preserve">Rotates game background and cover artwork - stills, GIFs and video - in Desktop and Fullscreen mode.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterRotation" xml:space="preserve">ROTATION</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterEnableRotation" xml:space="preserve">Enable rotation</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterEnableRotationHint" xml:space="preserve">Master switch. When off, ImageRotater does nothing and leaves your theme's own artwork handling untouched.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterTroubleshooting" xml:space="preserve">TROUBLESHOOTING</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterEnableDebug" xml:space="preserve">Enable debug logging</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterEnableDebugHint" xml:space="preserve">Writes ImageRotater.log next to the plugin's data. Leave off for normal use.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterBackgroundIntro" xml:space="preserve">Playnite's own background is always updated, which is what makes rotation work in every theme. A theme hosting the ImageRotater element gets GIF and video on top.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterEnableBackgrounds" xml:space="preserve">Enable background rotation</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterEnableBackgroundsHint" xml:space="preserve">Turns background rotation and animated background playback on or off without affecting covers.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterShape" xml:space="preserve">SHAPE</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterLetterbox" xml:space="preserve">Letterbox odd-shaped backgrounds</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterLetterboxHint" xml:space="preserve">When a game only has odd-shaped backgrounds (ultrawide banners, squares), they are pinned to the top of a screen-shaped canvas and fade into a blurred fill of themselves. The original files are never modified.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterLevelBackgrounds" xml:space="preserve">Level background sizes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterLevelBackgroundsHint" xml:space="preserve">Publishes every background for a game at one width. Playnite blurs the window background by a fixed amount after scaling, so backgrounds of different resolutions get visibly different blur - and switching between them makes the blur jump. Levelling the width removes that. The original files are never modified.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterWhenSeveral" xml:space="preserve">WHEN A GAME HAS SEVERAL</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterBackgroundSeveralHint" xml:space="preserve">Games with only one image are unaffected.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterPickSession" xml:space="preserve">Pick once per session</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterBackgroundPickSessionHint" xml:space="preserve">Chooses an image the first time you see a game and keeps it until Playnite restarts. Artwork stays put while you browse.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterPickEverySelection" xml:space="preserve">Pick again every time the game is selected</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterBackgroundPickEveryHint" xml:space="preserve">A different image each time you land on a game. Backgrounds rotate as you leave a game, so the change is never visible mid-switch.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterPickFixed" xml:space="preserve">Always use the same image</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterPickFixedHint" xml:space="preserve">Always shows the first image alphabetically. No rotation at all.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterSlideshow" xml:space="preserve">SLIDESHOW</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterChangeEvery" xml:space="preserve">Change every</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterBackgroundSlideshowHint" xml:space="preserve">While a game stays selected. 0 turns the slideshow off; anything below 5 is treated as off. Each change uses the transition chosen under Animation.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterBackgroundAnimation" xml:space="preserve">Background animation</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterBackgroundAnimationIntro" xml:space="preserve">How one still background gives way to the next. Videos and GIFs play through and keep their own fades.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterTransition" xml:space="preserve">TRANSITION</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterBackgroundTransitionHint" xml:space="preserve">How the background changes to the next still, in both Desktop and Fullscreen mode. A flash fills the whole screen here, so crossfade is the safe choice. A game needs two or more backgrounds for any of this to happen - with one there is nothing to change to.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterCrossfade" xml:space="preserve">Crossfade</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterFadeBlack" xml:space="preserve">Fade through black</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterFadeWhite" xml:space="preserve">Fade through white</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterCut" xml:space="preserve">Cut (no animation)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterCoverIntro" xml:space="preserve">Covers are managed separately from backgrounds: each game has its own covers folder, and cover art is chosen to match the shape of your grid cells rather than simply the largest image.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterEnableCovers" xml:space="preserve">Enable cover rotation</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterEnableCoversHint" xml:space="preserve">Off by default, since covers are usually curated deliberately.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterAnimateUnfocused" xml:space="preserve">Play animated covers on every visible tile, not just the selected one</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterAnimateUnfocusedHint" xml:space="preserve">Off by default for a reason: every animated tile decodes frames continuously, and Playnite is a 32-bit process. A library where many games have GIF or video covers can run it out of memory while scrolling. Videos outside the visible viewport are paused.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterVideoStart" xml:space="preserve">VIDEO START</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterVideoStartBeginning" xml:space="preserve">Start cover videos from the beginning</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterVideoStartBeginningHint" xml:space="preserve">Recommended for smoother navigation. Videos start at 0:00 and do not need an initial seek.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterVideoStartRandom" xml:space="preserve">Start cover videos at a random position</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterVideoStartRandomHint" xml:space="preserve">Desynchronises animated covers, but opening several videos at once can cause a small stutter because each video must seek after opening.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterCoverSeveralHint" xml:space="preserve">Covers rotate when you land on a game, and the grid tile updates in place.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterCoverPickSessionHint" xml:space="preserve">A fresh cover per Playnite launch. The grid stays calm while you browse.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterCoverPickEveryHint" xml:space="preserve">The tile changes each time you land on the game. Lively, but the grid reshuffles as you navigate.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterCoverSlideshowHint" xml:space="preserve">While a game stays selected. 0 turns the slideshow off; anything below 5 is treated as off. The selected game's tile changes in place, using the transition chosen under Animation.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterCoverAnimation" xml:space="preserve">Cover animation</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterCoverAnimationIntro" xml:space="preserve">How one still cover gives way to the next - the selected tile in a grid, or the cover in a details view. Videos and GIFs keep their own fades.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterCoverTransitionHint" xml:space="preserve">How a cover changes to the next still, in both Desktop and Fullscreen mode. Animated covers and videos keep their own fades. A game needs two or more covers for any of this to happen - with one there is nothing to change to.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterLibraryIntro" xml:space="preserve">Maintenance for the artwork ImageRotater already holds. Conversions replace each original only once its replacement exists, so an interrupted run leaves your library exactly as it was.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterConvert" xml:space="preserve">CONVERT</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterConvertGifs" xml:space="preserve">Convert all GIFs to MP4</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterConvertGifsHint" xml:space="preserve">Much smaller, and played by hardware rather than decoded frame by frame on the UI thread. Needs ffmpeg.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterConvertJpegs" xml:space="preserve">Convert all JPEGs to PNG</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterConvertJpegsHint" xml:space="preserve">Lossless, so no further quality is lost each time an image is processed - but the files get considerably larger. Quality already lost to JPEG does not come back.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterRepair" xml:space="preserve">REPAIR</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterRepairVideos" xml:space="preserve">Repair videos</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterRepairVideosHint" xml:space="preserve">Videos downloaded in a fragmented format show as solid black tiles even though nothing reports an error. This rewrites just the container - no quality loss, healthy videos untouched. Also available per game from the right-click menu. Needs ffmpeg.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterRepairVideosButton" xml:space="preserve">Repair videos (fix black tiles)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterRepairArtwork" xml:space="preserve">Repair artwork references</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterRepairArtworkHint" xml:space="preserve">If some games show solid black covers or backgrounds, they are pointing at plugin artwork that no longer exists - Playnite draws a missing image as black rather than as an empty tile. This clears those references so Playnite shows its own placeholder instead, and your library plugin can fetch the artwork again. Deletes nothing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterDangerZone" xml:space="preserve">DANGER ZONE</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterResetLibrary" xml:space="preserve">Reset library</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterResetLibraryHint" xml:space="preserve">Deletes every image and video ImageRotater holds for your whole library, and puts each game back to its own artwork. Your games keep the covers and backgrounds they had before the plugin touched them; anything downloaded through it is gone for good. You will be asked to confirm, and Playnite will offer to restart afterwards.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterResetLibraryButton" xml:space="preserve">Delete all plugin artwork and restore originals</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterMigrationIntro" xml:space="preserve">Bring artwork over from another plugin. Everything here copies; nothing is moved or deleted from the other plugin, and running an import again only adds what is new.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterBackgroundChanger" xml:space="preserve">BACKGROUNDCHANGER</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterImportBackgroundChanger" xml:space="preserve">Import artwork from BackgroundChanger</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterImportBackgroundChangerHint" xml:space="preserve">Copies every cover and background you gave BackgroundChanger into ImageRotater, game by game, so switching plugins keeps years of curation. Each game's images land in its own rotation straight away. Disable BackgroundChanger afterwards - the two cannot run together.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterImportWebPHint" xml:space="preserve">WebP files come across as they are. Playnite cannot show WebP, so run Library &gt; Maintenance &gt; Convert all GIFs to MP4 after importing to make them play (needs ffmpeg).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterSteam" xml:space="preserve">Steam</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterWebSearch" xml:space="preserve">Web search</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterYouTube" xml:space="preserve">YouTube</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterSteamSearchHelp" xml:space="preserve">Steam's own library artwork. Works for any game Steam sells, whichever store your copy came from. No key needed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterSgdbSearchHelp" xml:space="preserve">Curated game artwork, filtered by shape and style. Animated results need ffmpeg to preview.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterWebSearchHelp" xml:space="preserve">Any image on the web. Quality and shape vary, so check the size before picking.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterYouTubeSearchHelp" xml:space="preserve">Live wallpaper videos, saved as MP4. Needs yt-dlp, ffmpeg and deno - see the Setup tab in settings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterShapeAndSize" xml:space="preserve">Shape and size</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterStyle" xml:space="preserve">Style</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCImageRotaterGifConvertHint" xml:space="preserve">Smaller files, and smoother playback than an animated GIF.</sys:String>
